\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. THE voice that breathed o'er Eden,
\par That earliest wedding-day,
\par The primal marriage blessing,
\par It hath not passed away.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Still in the pure espousal
\par Of Christian man and maid
\par The Holy Three are with us,
\par The threefold grace is said,
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. For dower of blessed children,
\par For love and faith's sweet sake,
\par For high mysterious union
\par Which not on earth may break.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Be present, heavenly Father,
\par To give away this bride,
\par As Eve Thou gav'st to Adam
\par Out of his own pierced side.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Be present, gracious Saviour,
\par To join their loving hands,
\par As Thou didst bind two natures
\par In Thine eternal bands.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Be present, Holy Spirit,
\par To bless them as they kneel,
\par As Thou for Christ the Bridegroom
\par The heavenly spouse dost seal.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. O spread Thy pure wings o'er them!
\par Let no ill power find place,
\par When onward through life's journey
\par The hallowed path they trace,
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. To cast their crowns before Thee,
\par In perfect sacrifice,
\par Till to the home of gladness
\par With Christ's own bride they rise.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

